      "writtenOn": "2021-10-06T19:27:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So in order to use the experimental console, you need to be running the EC-3PO interperter and console. Commands get sent in an encapsulated form to the EC and the console utility (ec/util/ec3po/console.py) does the presentation of the console. I would think you want to add this feature there instead.\n\nBut also your commit message says that you won\u0027t be running servod, therefore you won\u0027t be running EC-3PO at all.\n\nFor more info about EC-3PO, see https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/HEAD/docs/ec-3po-design.md.",
      "revId": "d49fcfc6ab2b1b85c6c5689c48baf2949046b527",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01dd4679_0289566e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-06T20:43:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I think I understand: Enabling CONFIG_EXPERIMENTAL_CONSOLE strips out all the interactive console functionality (echo and so on) from the EC code, and instead expects commands to arrive in a special format preceded with two ampersands.  Even though I am not using servod, I could change my host-side code (OpenTitan tool) to emit the commands in this ampersand format.  (I have not read the EC-3PO document fully, but I expect that output from the commands also arrives in an encoded format, allowing it to be distinguished from general debug logging.)\n\nWith that, my concern about partial commands sitting in the buffer and causing problems would be addressed, as I assume that EC would recognize two ampersands \"in the middle\" of a command to mean that the previous partial command needs to be discarded, and parsing of a new command should begin.\n\nIf my understanding is correct, I can abandon this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "963a7563_a6c5b147",
      "revId": "d49fcfc6ab2b1b85c6c5689c48baf2949046b527",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f17a88f_d69efc89",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-06T21:34:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, that sounds about right. EC-3PO calculates a CRC of the command and if it fails, then the command is rejected. But note that this is for enhanced consoles only and I don\u0027t think any board defines this currently.",
      "parentUuid": "01dd4679_0289566e",
      "revId": "d49fcfc6ab2b1b85c6c5689c48baf2949046b527",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
