      "writtenOn": "2021-10-07T20:53:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will not be using servod or dut-control, this is for the OpenTitan project, and on the PC side will be a Rust program from the OpenTitan github repo.  I am contemplating replicating some EC-3PO logic in this Rust program, but before starting, I would like to fully understand the wire protocol, in particular, how does EC-3PO know when an executing command is done producing output, so that EC-3PO should present a new prompt on the client tty?  (As far as I can tell there is no replacement for ccputs(PROMPT) in case the enhanced console is enabled, so I wonder how EC-3PO could know when the previous command is done.)",
      "parentUuid": "5607ad82_2feb01fb",
      "revId": "d49fcfc6ab2b1b85c6c5689c48baf2949046b527",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
